Incremental Load Design
            Source Tables
                  |
                  v
            Read New/Changed Records
                  |
                  v
            Delta MERGE
                  |
                  v
            Bronze Tables
                  |
                  v
            Downstream Processing


In our project, data is read directly from Redshift tables into Azure Databricks using a Lakehouse architecture, eliminating the need for intermediate unload processes and file-based data movement.
The ingested data is stored in Bronze Delta tables as the raw data layer. It is then processed through Silver Delta tables, where data cleansing, standardization, and business matching rules are applied. The data is further enriched using fuzzy matching algorithms and eligibility classification logic to identify and categorize Contract Pharmacy relationships.
The final business-ready datasets are published to the Gold layer, providing curated and trusted data for reporting and analytics. Databricks Workflows orchestrate the end-to-end pipeline, including ingestion, cleansing, matching, classification, and publishing processes. Finally, Qlik Sense consumes the data directly from Databricks SQL views, enabling efficient and scalable reporting.

Full Load Logic
Used for:

Initial migration
Historical reload
Backfill
Reconciliation
Read Entire Source

df_844 = (
    spark.read
    .format("jdbc")
    .option("url", jdbc_url)
    .option("dbtable", "ARC_VIEW_844")
    .option("user", username)
    .option("password", password)
    .load()
)

df_867 = (
    spark.read
    .format("jdbc")
    .option("url", jdbc_url)
    .option("dbtable", "ARC_VIEW_867")
    .option("user", username)
    .option("password", password)
    .load()
)

######Load to Bronze

df_844.write \
    .format("delta") \
    .mode("overwrite") \
    .saveAsTable("bronze.arc_844")

df_867.write \
    .format("delta") \
    .mode("overwrite") \
    .saveAsTable("bronze.arc_867")
	
